(EXP-01: the four plain literal forms of the Literals table - integer, float,
 string and boolean - are all writable as a declaration initializer.
 Also covers: EXP-02, EXP-03, EXP-04, EXP-08.
 EXP-08 is the decimal-point claim: `0` declared as a number prints `0`,
 while `0.0` declared as a float prints `0.0`, so the point is what makes
 the literal a float and the float survives into the value.
 Booleans print as 1/0 - LANGUAGE.md:2364, not a defect of this section.
